@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title The six migration phases and what each one needs before it can start

start

:**Phase 0 — the conformance gate**
Measure the twelve cells: three capabilities
by search, vocabulary, detail, selection.
For each cell report whether a tool class exists,
whether anything is subscribed to dispatch it, and
where its route lives. Today that reads 6 live,
2 declared and dead, 1 borrowed, 3 absent;
note right
  Built first because it is the only thing that
  can say a later phase finished. Without a number
  that moves, "the map was rebuilt" is a claim
  nobody can check afterwards.
end note

fork
  :**Phase 1 — the tool contract in the library**
  One shape every capability tool satisfies, so
  search, vocabulary, detail and selection mean the
  same thing in all three capabilities. Each tool
  declares in source what the build reads to generate
  the registry: TOOL_DESCRIPTION, its subscriptions
  and may_call, and exactly one of
  UTTERANCE_MANAGER_PROMPT or NOT_UTTERANCE_ROUTABLE.
  ChatHealthyTool is the shape they build on;
fork again
  :**Phase 2 — collapse the three app.py into one gate**
  The per-service app.py files in FindCare,
  EvaluateCare and SharedServices become one generic
  gate module. The gate keeps no routes of its own:
  it collects the session token, HTTP head and
  GET/POST parameters — each if present — hands them
  to the UniversalNavigator, and streams the answer
  back. It is the only node that knows transport exists;
end fork

:**Phase 3 — the router becomes the UniversalNavigator**
The three inline branches — specialtySearch,
findAFacility, findAProvider — stop building httpx
calls and streaming events. The _OP_HANDLERS op-map
retires: the navigator reads the build's registry and
dispatches each of the five call types to whatever tool
subscribes to its route. A UniversalNavigatorProxy
fronts each satellite server; a finished tool returns
as an internal callback to the main, which owns the
render ledger, the serial deterministic merge, and
every session and timeout;
note right
  Needs Phase 1 for the contract the registry is
  generated from, and Phase 2 so the gate that
  reaches the navigator is at its final address.
end note

:**Phase 4 — fill and reshape the tools**
facility vocabulary, trial vocabulary and trial
detail do not exist. Facility detail is served by
ProviderDetailTool with entity_type=2 and gets its
own tool or a stated decision that sharing one is
correct. The classifier retires into the
UtteranceManager — preamble plus the registry's
fragments, one model call, the dispatch set back —
and user-facing prose becomes its own tool the
navigator dispatches with the facts;

:**Phase 5 — retire the rest of Code/**
Frontend shell, the iPhone tests, the
about-content files, Code/Shared and
Code/Shared/ops. Then the six build-tooling
paths change and the tree is deleted;

stop

floating note left
  Phase 0 is not a step in this sequence so much as
  the instrument the sequence is read with. Every
  phase below it ends by the conformance gate reporting
  a different number, and a phase that moves no number
  did not do what it said.
end note

@enduml
